er_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6690035417b0311c7a5b828f2e7dada84ecd3f71802fa8b88a897fe5e68d8f5f","event_uuid":"61ce034b-e599-4629-9885-d3b30ae59812","position":{"commit_sha":"3290fff75c8404a2b57a2c3c1f27a6beb6aa6181","position":"1785865949981850001-61ce034b-e599-4629-9885-d3b30ae59812"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"38f90ed2dc48b545605d9186d24196fe275861f51d2de5640b91c9daf1d81ce2","event_uuid":"0e0a913c-1711-4d5a-9999-57b68762116b","position":{"commit_sha":"d76c150747eb16b1fca0f591146f7822ce81f338","position":"1785867290224279001-0e0a913c-1711-4d5a-9999-57b68762116b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation COMPLETE; landing BLOCKED by a pre-existing, unrelated main-red condition.\n\nGerrit change: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1377 (e34a: config-drive Cloud probe resolved_statuses), Change-Id I399c2e88681c2ec6f6b0dc5dd055554da621cdda.\n\nWork done (all local gates green):\n- src/rebar/_config_schema.py: added JiraConfig.resolved_statuses: list[str] (default [\"Resolved\",\"Done\",\"Cancelled\"]) + _as_str_list coercer under _SECTIONS[\"jira\"]; REBAR_JIRA_RESOLVED_STATUSES auto-derived.\n- adapters/jira/probe.py: classify_probe_response now binds the configured set via _resolve_resolved_statuses(), falling back to module-level RESOLVED_STATUS_NAMES when unset/EMPTY/ConfigError (mirrors DC settings.py guard). DECISION comment updated.\n- docs/config.md: documented the new jira.resolved_statuses key.\n- tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/fetch/test_probe_resolved_statuses_config.py: held-out tests (7 passed).\n- make lint: PASS. make typecheck: PASS (429 files). Relevant test modules: 62 passed.\n\nHeld-out TDD + mutation evidence:\n- RED first: after adding only the config field, the two custom-set probe tests were RED for the right reason (probe ignored config -> \"Done\" stayed PRESENT_RESOLVED under a [\"Closed\",\"Complete\"] tenant). After threading config: GREEN (7 passed).\n- Mutation 1 \"return RESOLVED_STATUS_NAMES\" (ignore configured set): RED (2 custom-set tests). Restored -> GREEN.\n- Mutation 2 \"return frozenset(configured)\" (drop empty-list guard): RED (empty-list fallback test). Restored -> GREEN.\n\nBLOCKER (Verified -1, CI run 30934895074): origin/main is currently RED on the CI Module-size gate — src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py is 803 LOC (> 800 cap). The gate scans ALL src/rebar files globally, so every open Gerrit change gets Verified -1. This is unrelated to e34a (that file is untouched by 1377) and also fails main's own \"Test Suite (mirror)\" run 30934939148. Filed as bug ce14-01c6-a26f-4096 (discovered_from e34a; e34a depends_on it). Per the no-force rule and \"don't fix unrelated pre-existing issues\", e34a's change is NOT bundled with that repair and the ticket stays in_progress until main is green and 1377 reaches Verified +1.","timestamp":1785865949981850001}],"created_at":1785860409841206001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1a04966e-882e-4ed7-8a86-cf0be11a72c3","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"2127-348c-c41d-472e"},{"link_uuid":"d0e5df4c-09dd-46aa-ad36-6308e1138613","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3ac8-2107-c7c6-49b8"},{"link_uuid":"baac0202-0a28-4f95-9772-0350657ec73d","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"ce14-01c6-a26f-4096"},{"link_uuid":"0e0a913c-1711-4d5a-9999-57b68762116b","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"74a3-1213-9898-4195"},{"link_uuid":"6742e1f9-b41d-498f-9198-866067f4ea98","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4c31-a497-15ec-4584"}],"description":"Discovered while resolving item 3 of story 2127-348c-c41d-472e (probe resolved-status decision).\n\n## Problem\nCloud's absence probe hardcodes `RESOLVED_STATUS_NAMES = frozenset({'Resolved','Done','Cancelled'})` in `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/probe.py`. The DC side already sources its equivalent from config (`ReconcilerConfig.resolved_statuses`, `src/rebar/_config_schema.py`; consumed via `adapters/jira_datacenter/settings.py`). A Cloud tenant whose workflow uses non-standard resolved-status names (e.g. 'Closed', 'Complete', \"Won't Do\") has those issues MISCLASSIFIED as PRESENT_FILTERED instead of PRESENT_RESOLVED — with no way to fix it short of a code change.\n\n## Decision\nA runtime/config hook IS warranted for Cloud<->DC parity: Cloud should read a `jira.resolved_statuses` config key (defaulting to the current three names) the same way DC reads `reconciler.resolved_statuses`. This is already recorded as a repo-artifact comment at probe.py `RESOLVED_STATUS_NAMES`.\n\n## Plan\n1. `src/rebar/_config_schema.py`: add `resolved_statuses: list[str]` to the `JiraConfig` dataclass, defaulting via `field(default_factory=lambda: [\"Resolved\", \"Done\", \"Cancelled\"])`, mirroring `ReconcilerConfig.resolved_statuses`. Register the coercer `\"resolved_statuses\": _as_str_list` under `_SECTIONS[\"jira\"]` so the value is parsed from `[tool.rebar.jira]` and the `REBAR_JIRA_RESOLVED_STATUSES` env override is auto-derived (no canonical-name override needed).\n2. `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/probe.py`: resolve the resolved-status set from `load_config().jira.resolved_statuses` at classify time, keeping module-level `RESOLVED_STATUS_NAMES` as the fallback. Mirror DC's `settings.py` guard: fall back to the default when the configured list is EMPTY as well as unset or malformed (`ConfigError`) — bind `frozenset(configured) if configured else RESOLVED_STATUS_NAMES` inside a `try/except ConfigError`, since `_as_str_list` coerces `[]`/`[\"\"]` to `[]` without raising. `classify_probe_response` binds the resolved set into the shared `jira_family` classifier. Update the DECISION comment to note the hook now exists.\n3. `docs/config.md`: document the new `resolved_statuses` key in the `[tool.rebar.jira]` block.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `JiraConfig` exposes `resolved_statuses: list[str]` defaulting to `[\"Resolved\", \"Done\", \"Cancelled\"]`.\n- [ ] The key is coerced from `[tool.rebar.jira]` via `_as_str_list`, with `REBAR_JIRA_RESOLVED_STATUSES` auto-derived as its env override.\n- [ ] A tenant configuring `jira.resolved_statuses = [\"Closed\",\"Complete\"]` classifies a \"Closed\" issue as PRESENT_RESOLVED.\n- [ ] Under that same custom config, a \"Done\" issue (absent from the custom set) classifies as PRESENT_FILTERED, proving the configured set is consulted rather than merged with the default.\n- [ ] With the key unset, a \"Done\"/\"Resolved\"/\"Cancelled\" issue still classifies as PRESENT_RESOLVED via the module-level default fallback, so a stock DIG tenant is unaffected.\n- [ ] An explicitly empty configured list (`jira.resolved_statuses = []`) falls back to the module default rather than binding an empty set, mirroring DC's `settings.py` guard.\n- [ ] A held-out test pins the custom-name PRESENT_RESOLVED behavior and the default fallback; mutation-checked RED/GREEN.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass; the probe/config test modules are green.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_config_schema.py","reason":"Add resolved_statuses field to JiraConfig and register its coercer in _SECTIONS[jira]"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/probe.py","reason":"Thread configured jira.resolved_statuses through classify_probe_response, keeping RESOLVED_STATUS_NAMES as fallback"},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"Document the new jira.resolved_statuses config key"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/fetch/test_probe_resolved_statuses_config.py","reason":"Held-out tests pinning custom-name PRESENT_RESOLVED and default fallback"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","74a3-1213-9898-4195"],["depends_on","ce14-01c6-a26f-4096"],["relates_to","3ac8-2107-c7c6-49b8"],["relates_to","4c31-a497-15ec-4584"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"dac201d6-813d-4358-9324-416b68818883","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"e34a-1d0c-0daa-4f2c","ticket_type":"story","title":"Cloud probe RESOLVED_STATUS_NAMES should be configurable (parity with DC reconciler.resolved_statuses)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["3a62ec66-03a4-4671-9b86-6446629bb49a","1a04966e-882e-4ed7-8a86-cf0be11a72c3","d0e5df4c-09dd-46aa-ad36-6308e1138613","a562d371-2eed-448b-84b2-f26a841f3092","2520df2e-4ecd-48fc-af99-c85b1766bbe0","c5814443-3e86-428c-a76b-ca6ce5e4c2d9","c4c77a25-529b-4878-8f2a-aa4a6faa2979","ed0dd3f7-13dc-4707-beef-310182f312df","dac201d6-813d-4358-9324-416b68818883","69a93782-8f97-46e0-960a-ac642e4bf65f","baac0202-0a28-4f95-9772-0350657ec73d","61ce034b-e599-4629-9885-d3b30ae59812","0e0a913c-1711-4d5a-9999-57b68762116b","6742e1f9-b41d-498f-9198-866067f4ea98"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785867314399984539,"uuid":"022424f3-0c0a-4570-af44-e6d820584f56"}